    "description": "Specially crafted regular expressions could lead to memory corruption in the server. This could lead to Denial of Service, and could potentially be escalated to RCE. For more information, see https://www.ruby-lang.org/en/news/2026/10/23/regexp-fixes-for-gitlab-cves/\r\n\r\nIn Discourse, this is exploitable only by admin/moderator users. Therefore, this security advisory is primarily a concern for shared-hosting environments where admins may not be trusted.\r\n\r\nThis is resolved by a Ruby patch, which is available in `discourse/base:2.0.20261022-1808` and later. On a standard install, run `./launcher rebuild app` to get the latest version. Web-based updates will be unavailable until this rebuild has been completed.",
